  "narrative": {
    "intro": "QTC Medical Services reported $2.4B in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. QTC Medical Services received 58 awards this fiscal year, with an average award size of $40.7M, and obligations were down 18.3% year over year. QTC Medical Services earned the bulk of FY2026 obligations from the Department of Veterans Affairs, which obligated $2.3B. Historical obligations show year-by-year totals of FY21 $1B, FY22 $935M, FY23 $1.2B, FY24 $1.9B, and FY25 $2.9B. QTC Medical Services works primarily in healthcare NAICS markets, led by Offices of Physicians (except Mental Health Specialists) with $2.3B in obligations, followed by Offices of Physicians, Mental Health Specialists at $29.8M and All Other Outpatient Care Centers at $4.5M. Other federal buyers include the Department of Defense at $56.6M, the Department of the Interior at $3.5M, and the Department of Homeland Security at $2M. Current-year totals are partial, reported fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are QTC Medical Services' largest federal customers?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest customer, obligating $2.3B in FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense obligated $56.6M, the Department of the Interior obligated $3.5M, the Department of Homeland Security obligated $2M, and the Department of Justice obligated $1.4M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What services and NAICS markets does QTC Medical Services serve?",
        "body": "Offices of Physicians (except Mental Health Specialists) is the largest NAICS market, with $2.3B in FY2026 obligations. Offices of Physicians, Mental Health Specialists accounted for $29.8M, and All Other Outpatient Care Centers accounted for $4.5M."
      }
    ]
  },
